    {
      "line": 56,
      "upstream": "redirect to a FIFO whose reader drains slowly applies backpressure",
      "disposition": "case",
      "cases": [
        {
          "id": "file-io/redirect-to-slow-fifo",
          "template": ["", " reader.cjs out.fifo | echo ", " > out.fifo"],
          "values": [
            {
              "string": "{{NODE}}"
            },
            {
              "string": {
                "repeat": "z",
                "count": 204800
              }
            }
          ],
          "files": {
            "reader.cjs": "const fs = require('fs');\nconst fd = fs.openSync(process.argv[2], 'r');\nconst buf = Buffer.alloc(4096);\nlet zs = 0, total = 0;\nconst sleep = (ms) => Atomics.wait(new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4)), 0, 0, ms);\nsleep(200);\nfor (;;) { const n = fs.readSync(fd, buf, 0, buf.length, null); if (n === 0) break; total += n; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (buf[i] === 0x7a) zs++; if (total < 100000) sleep(1); }\nfs.writeFileSync('result.txt', JSON.stringify({ zs, total }));\n"
          },
          "setup": [
            {
              "template": ["mkfifo out.fifo"]
            }
          ],
          "platforms": ["posix"],
          "requires": ["node", "mkfifo"],
          "timeoutMs": 15000,
          "expect": {
            "files": {
              "result.txt": "{\"zs\":204800,\"total\":204801}"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "note": "upstream (test.concurrent.skipIf(!isPosix)) spawns a bun fixture that pre-fills the FIFO so the shell write hits EAGAIN, then drains it slowly and checks all 204800 \"z\" bytes arrive and exitCode 0. Reproduced with a slow node reader started first in a pipeline (reader sleeps 200ms before reading, so the 64 KiB pipe buffer fills and the shell must poll for writability); the reader writes its byte counts to result.txt. 204801 = payload + trailing newline of echo."
    },
